        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4ha",
          "text": "What Is Drowsy Driving?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4hd",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4hc",
          "text": "Drowsy driving is when a person operates a motor vehicle while too tired or fatigued to do so with the required level of attention, care and control. Driving while excessively drowsy can significantly affect the ability to drive safely. Common causes of drowsy driving include a lack of sleep, long or overnight drives, tight work schedules for career drivers, sleep disorders, and medication side effects.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b4hf",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s4he",
          "text": "Drowsy Driving Accident Statistics",
          "marks": []
        }
